description:
File: rust/lichen-gateway/src/discovery.rs
Lines: 120-132

The observe option encoding has redundant logic:
- Lines 123-124: When obs_val == 0, sets obs_value to &obs_bytes[3..4] which is [0]
- Line 131: Overrides to &[0u8][..] when obs_val == 0

Both produce identical output. The double-assignment is confusing.

Fix: Simplify to single conditional:
```rust
let obs_value: &[u8] = if obs_val == 0 {
    &[0u8]
} else if obs_val <= 0xFF {
    &obs_bytes[3..4]
} else if obs_val <= 0xFFFF {
    &obs_bytes[2..4]
} else if obs_val <= 0xFFFFFF {
    &obs_bytes[1..4]
} else {
    &obs_bytes[..]
};
```
